  "title": "Eureka",
  "media_type": "movie",
  "structured_data": {},
  "metadata_synthesis": "1983 surreal drama. Directed by Nicolas Roeg. Starring Gene Hackman. A bold, bizarre epic tracking the ecstasy of gold and the rot of wealth.",
  "setting_and_subculture": "Savage, freezing wilderness. Then a stagnant Caribbean paradise. Obscene idyll luxury. Surrounded by mobsters, social climbers, and hollow capitalism.",
  "visual_tone_and_feel": "Phantasmagoric. Blood splatter mixed with gold dust. Shimmering artificial stars. A literally cold opening. A stark, sun-drenched stagnation.",
  "media_era_tone": "1980s idiosyncratic cinema. Surreal but anchored. Unapologetically weird. An anti-epic critiquing ideological greed.",
  "pacing_and_structure": "A rapturous twenty-minute cold open. An abrupt leap forward. A massive reduction in speed. An incongruous, jarring final act.",
  "atmosphere_and_mood": "Euphoric discovery turning to decades of despair. Nightmarish adventure. Idle paranoia. The terrifying madness of endless wealth.",
  "themes_and_messages": "The curse of striking gold. Untrammelled capitalism. The hollow tragedy of having everything. The spiritual death that follows ultimate success.",
  "character_relationships": "A fading patriarch under siege from all sides. A contentious family. Philandering leeches. Greedy mobsters circling an aging king.",
  "lead_character_type": "A brutal prospector. A man who found pure ecstasy in dirt. An aging billionaire rotting in his own paradise.",
  "story_and_plot_type": "Tragedy of wealth. A fever-dream anti-epic. A dark descent into paranoia and mob violence over an island casino.",
  "who_and_when": "A crazed prospector. Mid-20th century. Men destroyed by their own endless capital.",
  "emotional_evocation": "Wordless joy. Crushing paranoia. Baffling tonal shifts. The creeping dread of a dream fully realized."
}
